  "word_count": 854,
  "body_markdown": "(310)-481-0111\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4® Dental Implants\n\nHybrid Fixed Detachable Denture\n\nZirconia Fixed Bridge\n\nImplant Supported Dentures\n\nRobotic Surgery\n\nCost & Compare\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nFAQ\n\nAesthetic Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers & Lumineers\n\nInvisalign\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nServices\n\nIV Sedation\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nSinus Augmentation\n\nTooth Extractions\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPeriodontics\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nMissing Teeth\n\nBone Loss\n\nFailing Dental Implants\n\nLoose Dentures\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nOur Facility\n\nPatient Stories\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\nWho We Are\n\nCommitment To Excellence\n\nMeet Dr. Tony Barriere\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nBlog\n\nContact Us\n\nPatient Portal\n\nNew Patients\n\nCurrent Patients\n\n\n# Category: Dental Implants\n\n\n\n## Are There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a safe and effective way to replace missing or damaged teeth. They are a permanent tooth replacement option that can help people restore their smile and give them back the confidence to speak, eat, and smile without worry. People can get treated with single dental implants, implant supported […]\n\n\n## Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a gold standard tooth replacement option that are surgically placed in a patient’s jawbone. A dental implant post is designed to act like a natural tooth root, giving patients a permanent and stable new smile. When people don’t replace their missing teeth with restorative dental implants, their […]\n\n\n## After My Smile Has Healed, How Is The Final Prosthesis Placed?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, CA are a gold standard tooth replacement option. The process of placing dental implants requires the dental implant post being strategically placed in the patient’s jawbone. After patients have healed from their dental implant surgery, the trusted dental professional can place the final prosthesis one them. The quality placement of […]\n\n\n## Is There A Difference Between A Temporary Prosthesis And A Final Prosthesis?\n\n\nA dental implant in Los Angeles, CA, is composed of a dental implant post, an abutment, and a prosthesis. After the dental implant post and abutment are securely placed, most patients are able to get a temporary prosthesis in the same surgical procedure. When the final prosthesis is ready, it can replace the temporary prosthesis […]\n\n\n## What Happens If I Don’t Have A Bone Grafting Procedure Before My Dental Implants Are Placed?\n\n\nWhen people have had one or more missing teeth for a long period of time, then they may need a bone grafting procedure before they can get treated with dental implants in Los Angeles, CA. A bone grafting procedure restores the patients jawbone density so it can support their new smile. Those who do not […]\n\n\n## After Getting A Full Arch Of Teeth Extracted, Should I Get Treated With Full Mouth Dental Implants?\n\n\nWhen people have a full arch of severely decayed or infected teeth, then they will want to go get those teeth extracted. After the damaged or infected teeth have been extracted, they will need to be replaced with full mouth dental implants. People will want to replace their extracted teeth with full mouth dental implants […]\n\n\n## Is There A Difference Between Implant Supported Dentures And Full Mouth Dental Implants?\n\n\nImplant supported dentures are a restorative tooth replacement option for those who no longer want to wear traditional dentures. Full mouth dental implants in Los Angeles, CA, also give patients a restored new smile that will last them for years to come. While implant supported dentures and full mouth dental implants can both restore the […]\n\n\n## Can Anyone Have A Temporary Prosthesis Placed After Having Dental Implant Surgery?\n\n\nWhen people have one or more missing or failing teeth, it will be hard for them to live their lives normally. With dental implants in Los Angeles, CA, however, most patients will be able to have their new smile in one day. Dental implants can give patients a new smile in one day when they […]\n\n\n## Are There Specific Parts That Make Up A Dental Implant?\n\n\nWhile people may know that dental implants are used to replace one or more missing teeth, they may not know the specific parts that make up a dental implant in Los Angeles, CA. Dental implants are composed of three main parts, the dental implant post, the abutment, and the dental crown/prosthesis. Here is what each […]\n\n\n## Are There Aesthetic And Functional Benefits To Getting Treated With Multiple Dental Implants?\n\n\nMultiple dental implants in Los Angeles, CA give several unique benefits for those who have missing or failing teeth. Not only do multiple dental implants give patients an aesthetically pleasing new smile, they can give patients a lot of functional benefits as well. With multiple dental implants, patients can have a beautiful new smile that […]\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Yelp Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddress:\n\n12301 Wilshire Blvd Suite 205,\n\nLos Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 481-0111\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nDental Website by Progressive Dental Marketing",
